        "rubric": [
          "Scientific accuracy",
          "Clarity and structure",
          "Use of examples",
          "Quality of expression"
        ],
        "modelAnswerGuide": "Space exploration is important because it expands scientific knowledge while driving technological progress on Earth. When scientists study other planets, stars, and cosmic systems, they gain insight into the origins of the Solar System, the conditions needed for life, and the physical laws governing the universe. At the same time, space programs often produce technologies that later benefit society, including improvements in materials science, satellite communication, weather forecasting, and remote sensing. These advances have practical value in transport, disaster management, agriculture, and global connectivity. Space exploration also encourages problem-solving at the highest level by requiring international collaboration, precision engineering, and long-term thinking. In this way, its significance is both scientific and human: it expands knowledge, strengthens innovation, and reminds societies that discovery remains one of the most powerful drivers of progress."
