        "prompt": "Evaluate the statement: \"climate resilience will shape the future more than most people realise.\"",
        "rubric": [
          "Scientific accuracy",
          "Clarity and structure",
          "Use of examples",
          "Quality of expression"
        ],
        "modelAnswerGuide": "Climate resilience matters because environmental change is already affecting weather patterns, water systems, agriculture, and public health. Scientifically, resilience refers to the ability of natural and human systems to absorb disruption, adapt effectively, and recover without collapsing. For example, climate-resilient cities may include better flood planning, heat-resistant infrastructure, and more reliable water systems. In ecosystems, resilience can be improved through biodiversity, habitat restoration, and reduced pollution. The importance of climate resilience lies in the fact that prevention alone is no longer enough; societies must also be prepared to respond intelligently to impacts that are already occurring. A resilient society is not one that avoids all change, but one that uses scientific evidence to adapt wisely. For that reason, climate resilience should be seen as a practical expression of applied science in service of long-term stability."
